/-!
# The Chern character on `K_0(Vect(X))` and its action on `CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐`

Let `(S, δ)` be the base situation of chapter 42 of the Stacks Project and let `X` be locally of
finite type over `S`. For a finite locally free `𝒪_X`-module `ℰ`, of a rank which need not be
constant, the Chern character has components `ch_p(ℰ) = P_p(ℰ)/p! ∈ A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐`, and by
[Stacks, Tag 0F9C] they are additive on short exact sequences. So `ℰ ↦ ch(ℰ)` extends additively
to the Grothendieck group:

  `ch : K_0(Vect(X)) ⟶ ∏_{p ≥ 0} A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐`,

the additive map underlying the ring map of [Stacks, Tag 0FEM].

A class `c ∈ A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐` acts on `CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐 = ⨁_k CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐` by capping on `X` itself, taking
`CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐` to `CH_{k-p}(X) ⊗ 𝐐`. On the fundamental class of a Noetherian `X` this is the map
`c ↦ c ∩ [X]` of [Stacks, Tag 0FEW].

The construction of the intersection product of [Stacks, Section 0FEX] uses that "Chern classes
commute": the operators `ch_p(ℰ) ∩ -` and `ch_q(ℱ) ∩ -` commute for all finite locally free `ℰ`,
`ℱ` and all `p`, `q`. Along any morphism `T ⟶ X` over which both modules have constant rank, the
power sums `P_p(ℰ)`, `P_q(ℱ)` restrict to elements of the commutative ring generated by Chern
classes ([Stacks, Tag 02UA]); by [Stacks, Tag 0FDZ] applied to the rank loci of `ℰ` and of `ℱ`,
this gives `P_p(ℰ) P_q(ℱ) = P_q(ℱ) P_p(ℰ)` in `∏_p A^p(X)`, and both being homogeneous, the
operators commute degree by degree.

When `δ_{X/S}` is bounded below, `CH_{k-p}(X) = 0` for `p` large, so the total operator
`ch(α) ∩ - = ∑_p ch_p(α) ∩ -` is a finite sum on each `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.chernCharacterVectorBundle` — `ch : K_0(Vect(X)) ⟶ ∏_p A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐`.
* `Stacks.Chow.rationalChowCap` — the operator `c ∩ -` on `CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐` of `c ∈ A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐`.
* `Stacks.Chow.rationalFundamentalClass` — the image of `[X]` in `CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐`.
* `Stacks.Chow.totalRationalChowCap` — the operator `∑_p c_p ∩ -` of `c ∈ ∏_p A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐`.
* `Stacks.Chow.chernCharacterCap`, `Stacks.Chow.rationalChernCharacterCap` — `ch(α) ∩ -` for
  `α ∈ K_0(Vect(X))` and for `α ∈ K_0(Vect(X)) ⊗ 𝐐`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.chernCharacterVectorBundle_classOf` — `ch([ℰ]) = ch(ℰ)`.
* `Stacks.Chow.rationalChowCap_rationalFundamentalClass` — `c ∩ [X]` is the map of Stacks 0FEW.
* `Stacks.Chow.commute_powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree` — `P_p(ℰ)` and `P_q(ℱ)` commute.
* `Stacks.Chow.commute_rationalChowCap_chernCharacterOfFiniteLocallyFree` — the operators
  `ch_p(ℰ) ∩ -` and `ch_q(ℱ) ∩ -` commute.
* `Stacks.Chow.commute_chernCharacterCap`, `Stacks.Chow.commute_rationalChernCharacterCap`,
  `Stacks.Chow.commute_rationalChowCap_chernCharacterCap` — the same for the total operators.
* `Stacks.Chow.totalRationalChowCap_lof_eq_sum` — for `δ_{X/S}` bounded below, the total operator
  is the sum over any large enough range of degrees.
* `Stacks.Chow.chernCharacterCap_one` — `ch(𝒪_X) ∩ -` is the identity.

## Implementation notes

The source states that `ch` is a ring map, by [Stacks, Tag 0F9D]. The multiplication of
`∏_p A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐` is not constructed here, so only the additive map is; that is all the action on
`CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐` needs.

The total operator must not depend on a chosen bound for `δ_{X/S}`. On `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐` it is the
sum over `p ≤ k - m`, with `m` the infimum of the values of `δ_{X/S}`
(`Stacks.Chow.capIndexBound`). For `δ_{X/S}` bounded below the omitted terms vanish
(`Stacks.Chow.totalRationalChowCap_lof_eq_sum`); otherwise the infimum is a junk value and the
operator has no meaning, though two total operators still commute, the set of pairs `(p, q)`
summed over being symmetric.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FEM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FEM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FEX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FEX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F9C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F9C)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FEW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FEW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FDZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FDZ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-! ### The Chern character on `K_0(Vect(X))` -/

section ChernCharacter

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]

/-- **The Chern character `ch : K_0(Vect(X)) ⟶ ∏_{p ≥ 0} A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐`**: the additive map sending
the class of a finite locally free module `ℰ`, of arbitrary rank, to
`(ch_0(ℰ), ch_1(ℰ), …)` with `ch_p(ℰ) = P_p(ℰ)/p!`; well defined by Stacks 0F9C. -/
def chernCharacterVectorBundle :
    VectorBundleKZero X →+ fullRationalChowCohomology C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX where
  toFun a p := ((Nat.factorial p : ℚ)⁻¹) ⊗ₜ[ℤ] powerSumKHom C sX p a p
  map_zero' := by
    funext p
    simp only [map_zero, TotalChowClass.zero_apply, TensorProduct.tmul_zero, Pi.zero_apply]
  map_add' a b := by
    funext p
    simp only [map_add, TotalChowClass.add_apply, TensorProduct.tmul_add, Pi.add_apply]

/-- `ch([ℰ]) = ch(ℰ)` for a finite locally free module `ℰ` of arbitrary rank. -/
theorem chernCharacterVectorBundle_classOf (E : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} E] (p : ℕ) :
    chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX (VectorBundleKZero.classOf X E) p =
      chernCharacterOfFiniteLocallyFree C sX E p := by
  change ((Nat.factorial p : ℚ)⁻¹) ⊗ₜ[ℤ] powerSumKHom C sX p (VectorBundleKZero.classOf X E) p = _
  rw [powerSumKHom_classOf]
  rfl

/-- The Chern character on `K_0(Vect(X)) ⊗ 𝐐`, the `𝐐`-linear extension of
`Stacks.Chow.chernCharacterVectorBundle`. -/
def rationalChernCharacterVectorBundle :
    ℚ ⊗[ℤ] VectorBundleKZero X →ₗ[ℚ]
      fullRationalChowCohomology C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX :=
  LinearMap.liftBaseChange ℚ (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX).toIntLinearMap

/-- `ch(r ⊗ α) = r ch(α)`. -/
theorem rationalChernCharacterVectorBundle_tmul (r : ℚ) (a : VectorBundleKZero X) :
    rationalChernCharacterVectorBundle C sX (r ⊗ₜ[ℤ] a) = r • chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX a :=
  LinearMap.liftBaseChange_tmul _ _ _ _

end ChernCharacter

/-! ### The cap operation on `CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐` -/

section Cap

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) (G : GysinSystem C) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S)
  [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]

local notation "CHQ" => DirectSum ℤ fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j

/-- Two `𝐐`-linear maps out of `CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐` agreeing on the classes `q ⊗ α`, `α ∈ CH_k(X)`, in
every degree are equal. -/
theorem rationalChowHomology_linearMap_ext {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [Module ℚ N]
    {f g : CHQ →ₗ[ℚ] N}
    (h : ∀ (k : ℤ) (q : ℚ) (α : chowGroup C sX k),
      f (DirectSum.of (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k (q ⊗ₜ[ℤ] α)) =
        g (DirectSum.of (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k (q ⊗ₜ[ℤ] α))) :
    f = g := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
  induction x using DirectSum.induction_on with
  | zero => rw [map_zero, map_zero]
  | of k t =>
    induction t using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
    | tmul q α => exact h k q α
    | add t t' ht ht' => rw [map_add, map_add, map_add, ht, ht']
  | add x y hx hy => rw [map_add, map_add, hx, hy]

/-- Classes of `CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐` given by heterogeneously equal Chow classes in equal degrees are
equal. -/
theorem of_tmul_eq_of_tmul_of_heq {i j : ℤ} (h : i = j) (q : ℚ) {x : chowGroup C sX i}
    {y : chowGroup C sX j} (hxy : x ≍ y) :
    DirectSum.of (fun l : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX l) i (q ⊗ₜ[ℤ] x) =
      DirectSum.of (fun l : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX l) j (q ⊗ₜ[ℤ] y) := by
  subst h
  obtain rfl := eq_of_heq hxy
  rfl

/-- The cap operation on `X` itself is additive in the class. -/
theorem chowCohomologyCap_add_apply (p : ℤ) (c d : chowCohomologyComponent C G sX p) (k : ℤ)
    (α : chowGroup C sX k) :
    chowCohomologyCap C G sX p (c + d) k α =
      chowCohomologyCap C G sX p c k α + chowCohomologyCap C G sX p d k α := by
  simp only [chowCohomologyCap, AddMonoidHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply,
    AddEquiv.coe_toAddMonoidHom, BivariantClass.add_cap, map_add]

/-- The cap operation `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐 ⟶ CH_{k-p}(X) ⊗ 𝐐` of a class of `A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐` on `X` itself,
the base change to `𝐐` of `Stacks.Chow.chowCohomologyCap`, as a `𝐐`-linear map in the class. -/
def rationalChowCapComponent (p k : ℤ) :
    rationalChowCohomologyComponent C G sX p →ₗ[ℚ]
      (ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX k →ₗ[ℚ] ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX (k - p)) :=
  LinearMap.liftBaseChange ℚ
    (AddMonoidHom.mk' (fun c => (chowCohomologyCap C G sX p c k).toIntLinearMap.baseChange ℚ)
      fun c d => by
        refine LinearMap.ext fun t => ?_
        induction t using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
        | tmul q α =>
          simp only [LinearMap.add_apply, LinearMap.baseChange_tmul,
            AddMonoidHom.coe_toIntLinearMap, ← TensorProduct.tmul_add, chowCohomologyCap_add_apply]
        | add t t' ht ht' => simp only [map_add, ht, ht']).toIntLinearMap

/-- `(r ⊗ c) ∩ (q ⊗ α) = (r q) ⊗ (c ∩ α)` in `CH_{k-p}(X) ⊗ 𝐐`. -/
theorem rationalChowCapComponent_tmul_tmul (p k : ℤ) (r : ℚ) (c : chowCohomologyComponent C G sX p)
    (q : ℚ) (α : chowGroup C sX k) :
    rationalChowCapComponent C G sX p k (r ⊗ₜ[ℤ] c) (q ⊗ₜ[ℤ] α) =
      (r * q) ⊗ₜ[ℤ] chowCohomologyCap C G sX p c k α := by
  simp only [rationalChowCapComponent, LinearMap.liftBaseChange_tmul, LinearMap.smul_apply,
    AddMonoidHom.coe_toIntLinearMap, AddMonoidHom.mk'_apply, LinearMap.baseChange_tmul,
    TensorProduct.smul_tmul', smul_eq_mul]

/-- **The cap operation of `c ∈ A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐` on `CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐 = ⨁_k CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐`**: on `X` itself,
taking `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐` to `CH_{k-p}(X) ⊗ 𝐐`, and `𝐐`-linear in `c`. -/
def rationalChowCap (p : ℤ) :
    rationalChowCohomologyComponent C G sX p →ₗ[ℚ] Module.End ℚ CHQ where
  toFun c := DirectSum.toModule ℚ ℤ CHQ fun k =>
    DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) (k - p) ∘ₗ
      rationalChowCapComponent C G sX p k c
  map_add' c d := DirectSum.linearMap_ext ℚ fun k => LinearMap.ext fun t => by
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.add_apply, DirectSum.toModule_lof, map_add]
  map_smul' r c := DirectSum.linearMap_ext ℚ fun k => LinearMap.ext fun t => by
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, DirectSum.toModule_lof, map_smul,
      RingHom.id_apply]

/-- The cap operation takes `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐` to `CH_{k-p}(X) ⊗ 𝐐`. -/
theorem rationalChowCap_lof (p : ℤ) (c : rationalChowCohomologyComponent C G sX p) (k : ℤ)
    (t : ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX k) :
    rationalChowCap C G sX p c (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) =
      DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) (k - p)
        (rationalChowCapComponent C G sX p k c t) := by
  simp only [rationalChowCap, LinearMap.coe_mk, AddHom.coe_mk, DirectSum.toModule_lof,
    LinearMap.comp_apply]

/-- The value of the cap operation: `(r ⊗ c) ∩ (q ⊗ α) = (r q) ⊗ (c ∩ α)`, in degree `k - p`. -/
theorem rationalChowCap_of_tmul (p : ℤ) (r : ℚ) (c : chowCohomologyComponent C G sX p) (k : ℤ)
    (q : ℚ) (α : chowGroup C sX k) :
    rationalChowCap C G sX p (r ⊗ₜ[ℤ] c)
        (DirectSum.of (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k (q ⊗ₜ[ℤ] α)) =
      DirectSum.of (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) (k - p)
        ((r * q) ⊗ₜ[ℤ] chowCohomologyCap C G sX p c k α) := by
  rw [← DirectSum.lof_eq_of ℚ, rationalChowCap_lof, rationalChowCapComponent_tmul_tmul,
    DirectSum.lof_eq_of]

/-- The cap operation vanishes on `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐` when no point of `X` has delta-dimension
`k - p`, the target `CH_{k-p}(X)` being zero. -/
theorem rationalChowCap_lof_eq_zero (p : ℤ) (c : rationalChowCohomologyComponent C G sX p) (k : ℤ)
    (t : ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX k)
    (hk : ∀ x : X, relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction sX x ≠ k - p) :
    rationalChowCap C G sX p c (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) =
      0 := by
  have hz : ∀ z : ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX (k - p), z = 0 := fun z => by
    induction z using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
    | tmul q y => rw [chowGroup_eq_zero C sX hk y, TensorProduct.tmul_zero]
    | add a b ha hb => rw [ha, hb, add_zero]
  rw [rationalChowCap_lof, hz (rationalChowCapComponent C G sX p k c t), map_zero]

/-! ### Compatibility with the fundamental class -/

/-- The image of the fundamental class `[X] ∈ CH_*(X)` in `CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐`. -/
def rationalFundamentalClass [IsNoetherian X] : CHQ :=
  TensorProduct.directSumRight ℤ ℚ ℚ (fun j : ℤ => chowGroup C sX j)
    ((1 : ℚ) ⊗ₜ[ℤ] totalFundamentalClass C sX)

/-- The image of `[X]` in `CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐` is `∑_n 1 ⊗ [X]_n`. -/
theorem rationalFundamentalClass_eq [IsNoetherian X] :
    rationalFundamentalClass C sX =
      ∑ n ∈ (fundamentalClassDegrees_finite C sX).toFinset,
        DirectSum.of (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) n
          ((1 : ℚ) ⊗ₜ[ℤ] fundamentalChowClass C sX n) := by
  rw [rationalFundamentalClass, totalFundamentalClass, TensorProduct.tmul_sum, map_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun n _ => ?_
  exact TensorProduct.directSumRight_tmul_lof ℤ ℚ (1 : ℚ) n _

/-- **Capping the fundamental class**: for `X` Noetherian, `c ∩ [X]` computed by the operator
`Stacks.Chow.rationalChowCap` is the map `A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐 ⟶ CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐`, `c ↦ c ∩ [X]`, of
Stacks 0FEW. -/
theorem rationalChowCap_rationalFundamentalClass [IsNoetherian X] (p : ℤ)
    (c : rationalChowCohomologyComponent C G sX p) :
    rationalChowCap C G sX p c (rationalFundamentalClass C sX) =
      rationalCapFundamentalClass C G sX sX (𝟙 X) (Category.id_comp sX) p c := by
  induction c using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | tmul r c =>
    rw [rationalCapFundamentalClass_tmul, rationalFundamentalClass_eq, map_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun n _ => ?_
    rw [rationalChowCap_of_tmul, mul_one, chowCohomologyCap_fundamentalChowClass]
    rfl
  | add x y hx hy => rw [map_add, LinearMap.add_apply, hx, hy, map_add]

/-! ### Commuting operators -/

/-- Two integral classes whose cap operations on `X` commute give commuting operators on
`CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐`, whatever the rational coefficients. -/
theorem commute_rationalChowCap_tmul {p q : ℤ} (c : chowCohomologyComponent C G sX p)
    (d : chowCohomologyComponent C G sX q)
    (h : ∀ (k : ℤ) (α : chowGroup C sX k),
      chowCohomologyCap C G sX p c (k - q) (chowCohomologyCap C G sX q d k α) ≍
        chowCohomologyCap C G sX q d (k - p) (chowCohomologyCap C G sX p c k α))
    (r r' : ℚ) :
    Commute (rationalChowCap C G sX p (r ⊗ₜ[ℤ] c)) (rationalChowCap C G sX q (r' ⊗ₜ[ℤ] d)) := by
  refine rationalChowHomology_linearMap_ext C sX fun k s α => ?_
  rw [Module.End.mul_apply, Module.End.mul_apply, rationalChowCap_of_tmul, rationalChowCap_of_tmul,
    rationalChowCap_of_tmul, rationalChowCap_of_tmul, show r * (r' * s) = r' * (r * s) by ring]
  exact of_tmul_eq_of_tmul_of_heq C sX (by ring) _ (h k α)

/-! ### The total cap operation -/

/-- The number of degrees summed over by the total cap operation on `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐`: the classes
of `A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐` for `p ≤ k - m` are used, `m` being the infimum of the values of `δ_{X/S}`;
when `δ_{X/S}` is bounded below, `CH_{k-p}(X) = 0` for the other `p`. -/
def capIndexBound (k : ℤ) : ℕ :=
  (k - sInf (Set.range (relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction sX))).toNat

/-- If `δ_{X/S}` is bounded below and a point has delta-dimension at most `k - n`, then `n` is
among the degrees summed over by the total cap operation on `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐`. -/
private theorem mem_range_capIndexBound_succ {Y : Scheme.{u}} (s : Y ⟶ C.S)
    (hb : BddBelow (Set.range (relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction s))) (x : Y) (k : ℤ) (n : ℕ)
    (h : relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction s x ≤ k - n) :
    n ∈ Finset.range (capIndexBound C s k + 1) := by
  rw [Finset.mem_range, capIndexBound]
  have := csInf_le hb ⟨x, rfl⟩
  omega

/-- **The total cap operation `c ↦ ∑_p c_p ∩ -`** of a family `c ∈ ∏_{p ≥ 0} A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐`, on
`CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐`: on `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐` it is the sum over `p ≤ k - m`, `m` the infimum of
`δ_{X/S}`, which for `δ_{X/S}` bounded below is the sum over all `p`
(`Stacks.Chow.totalRationalChowCap_lof_eq_sum`). -/
def totalRationalChowCap : fullRationalChowCohomology C G sX →ₗ[ℚ] Module.End ℚ CHQ where
  toFun c := DirectSum.toModule ℚ ℤ CHQ fun k =>
    ∑ p ∈ Finset.range (capIndexBound C sX k + 1),
      rationalChowCap C G sX p (c p) ∘ₗ DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k
  map_add' c d := DirectSum.linearMap_ext ℚ fun k => LinearMap.ext fun t => by
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.add_apply, DirectSum.toModule_lof,
      LinearMap.sum_apply, Pi.add_apply, map_add, Finset.sum_add_distrib]
  map_smul' r c := DirectSum.linearMap_ext ℚ fun k => LinearMap.ext fun t => by
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, DirectSum.toModule_lof,
      LinearMap.sum_apply, Pi.smul_apply, map_smul, Finset.smul_sum,
      RingHom.id_apply]

/-- On `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐` the total cap operation is the sum of the `c_p ∩ -` for
`p ≤ Stacks.Chow.capIndexBound C sX k`. -/
theorem totalRationalChowCap_lof (c : fullRationalChowCohomology C G sX) (k : ℤ)
    (t : ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX k) :
    totalRationalChowCap C G sX c (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) =
      ∑ p ∈ Finset.range (capIndexBound C sX k + 1),
        rationalChowCap C G sX p (c p)
          (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) := by
  simp only [totalRationalChowCap, LinearMap.coe_mk, AddHom.coe_mk, DirectSum.toModule_lof,
    LinearMap.sum_apply, LinearMap.comp_apply]

/-- **The total cap operation is the sum over all relevant degrees**: if `δ_{X/S}` is bounded
below, then on `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐` it is the sum over any finite set of degrees `p` containing those
for which some point of `X` has delta-dimension `k - p`. -/
theorem totalRationalChowCap_lof_eq_sum_of_bddBelow
    (hb : BddBelow (Set.range (relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction sX)))
    (c : fullRationalChowCohomology C G sX) (k : ℤ) (t : ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX k)
    (s : Finset ℕ)
    (hs : ∀ (p : ℕ) (x : X), relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction sX x = k - p → p ∈ s) :
    totalRationalChowCap C G sX c (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) =
      ∑ p ∈ s, rationalChowCap C G sX p (c p)
        (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) := by
  rw [totalRationalChowCap_lof]
  refine ((Finset.sum_subset Finset.inter_subset_left fun p hp hn => ?_).symm).trans
    (Finset.sum_subset Finset.inter_subset_right fun p hp hn => ?_)
  · refine rationalChowCap_lof_eq_zero C G sX p _ k t fun x hx => hn ?_
    exact Finset.mem_inter.2 ⟨hp, hs p x hx⟩
  · refine rationalChowCap_lof_eq_zero C G sX p _ k t fun x hx => hn ?_
    exact Finset.mem_inter.2 ⟨mem_range_capIndexBound_succ C sX hb x k p hx.le, hp⟩

/-- **The total cap operation for `δ_{X/S}` bounded below by `lo`**: on `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐` it is the
sum over any finite set of degrees containing all `p ≤ k - lo`. -/
theorem totalRationalChowCap_lof_eq_sum (lo : ℤ)
    (hlo : ∀ x : X, lo ≤ relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction sX x)
    (c : fullRationalChowCohomology C G sX) (k : ℤ) (t : ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX k)
    (s : Finset ℕ) (hs : ∀ p : ℕ, (p : ℤ) ≤ k - lo → p ∈ s) :
    totalRationalChowCap C G sX c (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) =
      ∑ p ∈ s, rationalChowCap C G sX p (c p)
        (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) :=
  totalRationalChowCap_lof_eq_sum_of_bddBelow C G sX ⟨lo, Set.forall_mem_range.2 hlo⟩ c
    k t s fun p x hx => hs p (by have := hlo x; omega)

/-- The total cap operation for `δ_{X/S}` bounded below by `lo` is the sum over `p ≤ N` for any
`N ≥ k - lo`. -/
theorem totalRationalChowCap_lof_eq_sum_range (lo : ℤ)
    (hlo : ∀ x : X, lo ≤ relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction sX x)
    (c : fullRationalChowCohomology C G sX) (k : ℤ) (t : ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX k) (N : ℕ)
    (hN : k - lo ≤ N) :
    totalRationalChowCap C G sX c (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) =
      ∑ p ∈ Finset.range (N + 1), rationalChowCap C G sX p (c p)
        (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) :=
  totalRationalChowCap_lof_eq_sum C G sX lo hlo c k t _ fun p hp => by
    rw [Finset.mem_range]
    omega

/-- **Total cap operations of families whose components commute commute.** No bound on
`δ_{X/S}` is needed: on `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐` both composites are the sum over the same symmetric set of
pairs of degrees. -/
theorem commute_totalRationalChowCap (c d : fullRationalChowCohomology C G sX)
    (h : ∀ p q : ℕ, Commute (rationalChowCap C G sX p (c p)) (rationalChowCap C G sX q (d q))) :
    Commute (totalRationalChowCap C G sX c) (totalRationalChowCap C G sX d) := by
  refine DirectSum.linearMap_ext ℚ fun k => LinearMap.ext fun t => ?_
  have key : ∀ (e e' : fullRationalChowCohomology C G sX) (q : ℕ),
      totalRationalChowCap C G sX e (rationalChowCap C G sX q (e' q)
          (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t)) =
        ∑ p ∈ Finset.range (capIndexBound C sX (k - q) + 1),
          rationalChowCap C G sX p (e p) (rationalChowCap C G sX q (e' q)
            (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t)) := by
    intro e e' q
    rw [rationalChowCap_lof, totalRationalChowCap_lof]
  rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.comp_apply, Module.End.mul_apply, Module.End.mul_apply,
    totalRationalChowCap_lof, totalRationalChowCap_lof, map_sum, map_sum,
    Finset.sum_congr rfl fun q _ => key c d q, Finset.sum_congr rfl fun p _ => key d c p]
  refine (Finset.sum_comm' fun q p => ?_).trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun p _ =>
    Finset.sum_congr rfl fun q _ => congrArg (fun φ : Module.End ℚ CHQ =>
      φ (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t)) (h p q).eq)
  simp only [Finset.mem_range, capIndexBound]
  omega

/-- **A cap operation commuting with the components of a family commutes with its total cap
operation**, for `δ_{X/S}` bounded below. -/
theorem commute_rationalChowCap_totalRationalChowCap (lo : ℤ)
    (hlo : ∀ x : X, lo ≤ relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction sX x) (p : ℕ)
    (y : rationalChowCohomologyComponent C G sX p) (d : fullRationalChowCohomology C G sX)
    (h : ∀ q : ℕ, Commute (rationalChowCap C G sX p y) (rationalChowCap C G sX q (d q))) :
    Commute (rationalChowCap C G sX p y) (totalRationalChowCap C G sX d) := by
  have hb : BddBelow (Set.range (relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction sX)) :=
    ⟨lo, Set.forall_mem_range.2 hlo⟩
  refine DirectSum.linearMap_ext ℚ fun k => LinearMap.ext fun t => ?_
  rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.comp_apply, Module.End.mul_apply, Module.End.mul_apply,
    totalRationalChowCap_lof, map_sum, rationalChowCap_lof C G sX p y k t,
    totalRationalChowCap_lof_eq_sum_of_bddBelow C G sX hb d (k - p) _
      (Finset.range (capIndexBound C sX k + 1)), ← rationalChowCap_lof C G sX p y k t]
  · exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun q _ => by
      rw [← Module.End.mul_apply, (h q).eq, Module.End.mul_apply]
  · intro q x hx
    exact mem_range_capIndexBound_succ C sX hb x k q (by omega)

end Cap

/-! ### Commutation of the power sums -/

section PowerSum

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]

/-- **Homogeneous commuting total classes have commuting operations**: if `a` and `b` are
homogeneous of degrees `i` and `j` and commute in `∏_p A^p(X)`, then `a_i ∩ (b_j ∩ α)` and
`b_j ∩ (a_i ∩ α)` agree on every test scheme. -/
theorem TotalChowClass.op_op_heq_of_commute {a b : TotalChowClass C sX} {i j : ℕ}
    (ha : TotalChowClass.IsHomogeneous i a) (hb : TotalChowClass.IsHomogeneous j b)
    (hab : Commute a b) {T : Scheme.{u}} (g : T ⟶ X) [LocallyOfFiniteType g] (k : ℤ)
    (α : chowGroup C (g ≫ sX) k) :
    a.op g (k - j) i (b.op g k j α) ≍ b.op g (k - i) j (a.op g k i α) := by
  have hc : a.op g * b.op g = b.op g * a.op g := by
    rw [← TotalChowClass.op_mul, ← TotalChowClass.op_mul, hab.eq]
  have h1 := gradedCap_mul_apply_of_isHomogeneous (ha.op g) (hb.op g) k (m := i + j) rfl α
  have h2 := gradedCap_mul_apply_of_isHomogeneous (hb.op g) (ha.op g) k (m := i + j)
    (Nat.add_comm i j) α
  rw [hc] at h1
  have h3 := h1.symm.trans h2
  rw [capTo_def, capTo_def] at h3
  exact (gradedDegreeCast_heq _ _).symm.trans ((heq_of_eq h3).trans (gradedDegreeCast_heq _ _))

/-- Homogeneous commuting total classes have commuting cap operations on `CH_*(X)`. -/
theorem chowCohomologyCap_chowCohomologyCap_heq_of_commute {a b : TotalChowClass C sX} {i j : ℕ}
    (ha : TotalChowClass.IsHomogeneous i a) (hb : TotalChowClass.IsHomogeneous j b)
    (hab : Commute a b) (k : ℤ) (α : chowGroup C sX k) :
    chowCohomologyCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX i (a i) (k - j)
        (chowCohomologyCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX j (b j) k α) ≍
      chowCohomologyCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX j (b j) (k - i)
        (chowCohomologyCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX i (a i) k α) := by
  have e : ∀ (p : ℕ) (c : TotalChowClass C sX) (l : ℤ) (y : chowGroup C sX l),
      chowGroupCongr C (Category.id_comp sX).symm (l - p)
          (chowCohomologyCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX p (c p) l y) =
        c.op (𝟙 X) l p (chowGroupCongr C (Category.id_comp sX).symm l y) :=
    fun p c l y => eq_of_heq ((chowGroupCongr_heq _ _ _ _).trans
      (chowCohomologyCap_heq_idRule_ofGysinSystem C _ sX p (c p) l y))
  refine (chowCohomologyCap_heq_idRule_ofGysinSystem C _ sX i (a i) (k - j) _).trans ?_
  refine HEq.trans ?_ (chowCohomologyCap_heq_idRule_ofGysinSystem C _ sX j (b j) (k - i) _).symm
  change a.op (𝟙 X) (k - j) i _ ≍ b.op (𝟙 X) (k - i) j _
  rw [e j b k α, e i a k α]
  exact TotalChowClass.op_op_heq_of_commute C sX ha hb hab (𝟙 X) k _

variable (E F : X.Modules) [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} E]
  [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} F]

/-- **Power sums of modules of arbitrary ranks commute**: `P_p(ℰ) P_q(ℱ) = P_q(ℱ) P_p(ℰ)` in
`∏_r A^r(X)`. Along a morphism over which both modules have constant rank both restrict into the
commutative ring of Chern classes (Stacks 02UA), and by Stacks 0FDZ, applied to the rank loci of
`ℰ` and of `ℱ`, that determines the products. -/
theorem commute_powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree (p q : ℕ) :
    Commute (powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree C sX E p) (powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree C sX F q) := by
  refine TotalChowClass.eq_of_res_eq_of_constantRank₂ C sX E F
    fun {T sT _} g _ hs r s hr hs' => ?_
  have := hr
  have := hs'
  rw [map_mul, map_mul, res_powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree_of_rank C sX E g hs r,
    res_powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree_of_rank C sX F g hs s]
  exact (commute_powerSumTotal C sT _ _ r s p q).eq

/-- `P_p(ℰ)` is homogeneous of degree `p`, for `ℰ` of arbitrary rank. -/
theorem isHomogeneous_powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree (p : ℕ) :
    TotalChowClass.IsHomogeneous p (powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree C sX E p) := by
  have h : TotalChowClass.homComponent p (powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree C sX E p) =
      powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree C sX E p := by
    refine TotalChowClass.eq_of_res_eq (isClopenDecomposition_rankLociFamily E) fun r => ?_
    have := isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_pullback_rankLociFamily E r
    rw [TotalChowClass.res_homComponent, res_powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree_rankLocus]
    exact homPart_powerSumTotal C _ _ r.down p
  rw [← h]
  exact TotalChowClass.isHomogeneous_homComponent p _

/-- **"Chern classes commute"** (the step of Stacks 0FEX): for finite locally free modules `ℰ`,
`ℱ` of arbitrary ranks and all `p`, `q`, the operators `ch_p(ℰ) ∩ -` and `ch_q(ℱ) ∩ -` on
`CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐` commute. -/
theorem commute_rationalChowCap_chernCharacterOfFiniteLocallyFree (p q : ℕ) :
    Commute
      (rationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX p
        (chernCharacterOfFiniteLocallyFree C sX E p))
      (rationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX q
        (chernCharacterOfFiniteLocallyFree C sX F q)) :=
  commute_rationalChowCap_tmul C _ sX _ _
    (chowCohomologyCap_chowCohomologyCap_heq_of_commute C sX
      (isHomogeneous_powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree C sX E p)
      (isHomogeneous_powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree C sX F q)
      (commute_powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree C sX E F p q)) _ _

end PowerSum

/-! ### The action of the Chern character -/

section ChernCharacterCap

variable (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (sX : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType sX]

local notation "CHQ" => DirectSum ℤ fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j

/-- **"Chern classes commute", in `K_0(Vect(X))`**: for all `α, β ∈ K_0(Vect(X))` and all `p`,
`q`, the operators `ch_p(α) ∩ -` and `ch_q(β) ∩ -` on `CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐` commute. -/
theorem commute_rationalChowCap_chernCharacterVectorBundle (a b : VectorBundleKZero X)
    (p q : ℕ) :
    Commute
      (rationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX p (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX a p))
      (rationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX q
        (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX b q)) := by
  let φ : VectorBundleKZero X →+ Module.End ℚ CHQ :=
    (rationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX p).toAddMonoidHom.comp
      ((Pi.evalAddMonoidHom _ p).comp (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX))
  let ψ : VectorBundleKZero X →+ Module.End ℚ CHQ :=
    (rationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX q).toAddMonoidHom.comp
      ((Pi.evalAddMonoidHom _ q).comp (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX))
  have hstep : ∀ M : X.Modules,
      Stacks.FiniteLocallyFree.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} (R := X.ringCatSheaf) M →
        ∀ c, φ (VectorBundleKZero.classOf X M) * ψ c =
          ψ c * φ (VectorBundleKZero.classOf X M) := by
    intro M hM c
    refine DFunLike.congr_fun (VectorBundleKZero.addHom_ext
      (φ := (AddMonoidHom.mulLeft (φ (VectorBundleKZero.classOf X M))).comp ψ)
      (ψ := (AddMonoidHom.mulRight (φ (VectorBundleKZero.classOf X M))).comp ψ)
      fun N hN => ?_) c
    change rationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX p
        (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX (VectorBundleKZero.classOf X M) p) *
      rationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX q
        (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX (VectorBundleKZero.classOf X N) q) =
      rationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX q
        (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX (VectorBundleKZero.classOf X N) q) *
      rationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX p
        (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX (VectorBundleKZero.classOf X M) p)
    rw [chernCharacterVectorBundle_classOf, chernCharacterVectorBundle_classOf]
    exact (commute_rationalChowCap_chernCharacterOfFiniteLocallyFree C sX M N p q).eq
  exact DFunLike.congr_fun (VectorBundleKZero.addHom_ext
    (φ := (AddMonoidHom.mulRight (ψ b)).comp φ)
    (ψ := (AddMonoidHom.mulLeft (ψ b)).comp φ) fun M hM => hstep M hM b) a

/-- **`ch(α) ∩ -` on `CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐`** for `α ∈ K_0(Vect(X))`: the total cap operation of
`ch(α) ∈ ∏_p A^p(X) ⊗ 𝐐`. For `δ_{X/S}` bounded below, it is `∑_p ch_p(α) ∩ -`, a finite sum on
each `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐` (`Stacks.Chow.chernCharacterCap_lof_eq_sum`). -/
def chernCharacterCap (a : VectorBundleKZero X) : Module.End ℚ CHQ :=
  totalRationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX a)

/-- On `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐`, `ch(α) ∩ -` is the sum of the `ch_p(α) ∩ -` for
`p ≤ Stacks.Chow.capIndexBound C sX k`. -/
theorem chernCharacterCap_lof (a : VectorBundleKZero X) (k : ℤ) (t : ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX k) :
    chernCharacterCap C sX a (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) =
      ∑ p ∈ Finset.range (capIndexBound C sX k + 1),
        rationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX p (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX a p)
          (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) :=
  totalRationalChowCap_lof C _ sX _ k t

/-- For `δ_{X/S}` bounded below by `lo`, `ch(α) ∩ -` on `CH_k(X) ⊗ 𝐐` is `∑_p ch_p(α) ∩ -` over
any finite set of degrees containing all `p ≤ k - lo`. -/
theorem chernCharacterCap_lof_eq_sum (lo : ℤ)
    (hlo : ∀ x : X, lo ≤ relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction sX x)
    (a : VectorBundleKZero X) (k : ℤ) (t : ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX k) (s : Finset ℕ)
    (hs : ∀ p : ℕ, (p : ℤ) ≤ k - lo → p ∈ s) :
    chernCharacterCap C sX a (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) =
      ∑ p ∈ s, rationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX p
        (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX a p)
          (DirectSum.lof ℚ ℤ (fun j : ℤ => ℚ ⊗[ℤ] chowGroup C sX j) k t) :=
  totalRationalChowCap_lof_eq_sum C _ sX lo hlo _ k t s hs

/-- `α ↦ ch(α) ∩ -`, as an additive map `K_0(Vect(X)) ⟶ End(CH_*(X) ⊗ 𝐐)`. -/
def chernCharacterCapHom : VectorBundleKZero X →+ Module.End ℚ CHQ :=
  (totalRationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX).toAddMonoidHom.comp
    (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX)

/-- The additive map `Stacks.Chow.chernCharacterCapHom` evaluates to `ch(α) ∩ -`. -/
theorem chernCharacterCapHom_apply (a : VectorBundleKZero X) :
    chernCharacterCapHom C sX a = chernCharacterCap C sX a :=
  rfl

/-- **`ch(α) ∩ -` for `α ∈ K_0(Vect(X)) ⊗ 𝐐`**, the `𝐐`-linear extension of
`Stacks.Chow.chernCharacterCap`. -/
def rationalChernCharacterCap : ℚ ⊗[ℤ] VectorBundleKZero X →ₗ[ℚ] Module.End ℚ CHQ :=
  totalRationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX ∘ₗ rationalChernCharacterVectorBundle C sX

/-- `ch(r ⊗ α) ∩ - = r (ch(α) ∩ -)`. -/
theorem rationalChernCharacterCap_tmul (r : ℚ) (a : VectorBundleKZero X) :
    rationalChernCharacterCap C sX (r ⊗ₜ[ℤ] a) = r • chernCharacterCap C sX a := by
  rw [rationalChernCharacterCap, LinearMap.comp_apply, rationalChernCharacterVectorBundle_tmul,
    map_smul]
  rfl

/-- **The operators `ch(α) ∩ -` and `ch(β) ∩ -` commute**, for all `α, β ∈ K_0(Vect(X))`. -/
theorem commute_chernCharacterCap (a b : VectorBundleKZero X) :
    Commute (chernCharacterCap C sX a) (chernCharacterCap C sX b) :=
  commute_totalRationalChowCap C _ sX _ _ fun p q =>
    commute_rationalChowCap_chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX a b p q

/-- **The operators `ch(α) ∩ -` and `ch(β) ∩ -` commute**, for all `α, β ∈ K_0(Vect(X)) ⊗ 𝐐`. -/
theorem commute_rationalChernCharacterCap (x y : ℚ ⊗[ℤ] VectorBundleKZero X) :
    Commute (rationalChernCharacterCap C sX x) (rationalChernCharacterCap C sX y) := by
  induction x using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | add x x' hx hx' => rw [map_add]; exact hx.add_left hx'
  | tmul r a =>
    induction y using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
    | add y y' hy hy' => rw [map_add]; exact hy.add_right hy'
    | tmul r' b =>
      rw [rationalChernCharacterCap_tmul, rationalChernCharacterCap_tmul]
      exact ((commute_chernCharacterCap C sX a b).smul_left r).smul_right r'

/-- **The operators `ch_p(α) ∩ -` and `ch(β) ∩ -` commute**, for `α, β ∈ K_0(Vect(X))` and
`δ_{X/S}` bounded below. -/
theorem commute_rationalChowCap_chernCharacterCap (lo : ℤ)
    (hlo : ∀ x : X, lo ≤ relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction sX x)
    (a b : VectorBundleKZero X) (p : ℕ) :
    Commute
      (rationalChowCap C (gysinSystemOfInvertible C) sX p (chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX a p))
      (chernCharacterCap C sX b) :=
  commute_rationalChowCap_totalRationalChowCap C _ sX lo hlo p _ _ fun q =>
    commute_rationalChowCap_chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX a b p q

/-! ### The unit -/

/-- The degree-`1` part of the class `1` vanishes. -/
theorem TotalChowClass.homPart_one_one :
    TotalChowClass.homComponent 1 (1 : TotalChowClass C sX) = 0 :=
  TotalChowClass.ext fun q => by
    rw [TotalChowClass.homComponent_apply]
    split_ifs with hq
    · subst hq
      exact TotalChowClass.one_apply_of_ne one_ne_zero
    · rfl

variable (M : X.Modules) [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.{u, u, u} M 1]
  (e : M ≅ SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)

include e in
/-- `P_p(𝒪_X) = 0` for `p > 0`, for any module isomorphic to `𝒪_X`. -/
theorem powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree_eq_zero_of_iso_unit
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} M] {p : ℕ} (hp : p ≠ 0) :
    powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree C sX M p = 0 := by
  rw [powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree_eq_powerSumTotal C sX M 1, powerSumTotal_of_rank_one,
    totalChern_eq_one_of_iso_unit C sX M e, TotalChowClass.homPart_one_one, zero_pow hp]

include e in
/-- **`ch(𝒪_X) ∩ -` is the identity**, for any module isomorphic to `𝒪_X`: `ch_0(𝒪_X) = 1` and
`ch_p(𝒪_X) = 0` for `p > 0`. -/
theorem chernCharacterCap_classOf_of_iso_unit :
    chernCharacterCap C sX (VectorBundleKZero.classOf X M) = 1 := by
  have := SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.isFiniteLocallyFree M 1
  have h0 : chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX (VectorBundleKZero.classOf X M) 0 =
      (1 : ℚ) ⊗ₜ[ℤ] (1 : TotalChowClass C sX) 0 := by
    rw [chernCharacterVectorBundle_classOf, chernCharacterOfFiniteLocallyFree,
      powerSumClassOfFiniteLocallyFree, powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree_eq_powerSumTotal C sX M 1,
      powerSumTotal_zero, Nat.cast_one, Nat.factorial_zero, Nat.cast_one, inv_one]
  have hp : ∀ p : ℕ, p ≠ 0 →
      chernCharacterVectorBundle C sX (VectorBundleKZero.classOf X M) p = 0 := by
    intro p hp
    rw [chernCharacterVectorBundle_classOf, chernCharacterOfFiniteLocallyFree,
      powerSumClassOfFiniteLocallyFree,
      powerSumOfFiniteLocallyFree_eq_zero_of_iso_unit C sX M e hp, TotalChowClass.zero_apply,
      TensorProduct.tmul_zero]
  refine DirectSum.linearMap_ext ℚ fun k => LinearMap.ext fun t => ?_
  rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.comp_apply, Module.End.one_apply, chernCharacterCap_lof,
    Finset.sum_eq_single 0 (fun p _ hp' => by rw [hp p hp', map_zero, LinearMap.zero_apply])
      (fun h => absurd (Finset.mem_range.2 (Nat.succ_pos _)) h), h0]
  induction t using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | add t t' ht ht' => rw [map_add, map_add, ht, ht']
  | tmul q α =>
    rw [DirectSum.lof_eq_of, rationalChowCap_of_tmul, one_mul]
    refine of_tmul_eq_of_tmul_of_heq C sX (by simp) q ?_
    refine (chowCohomologyCap_heq_idRule_ofGysinSystem C _ sX _ _ k α).trans ?_
    change (1 : TotalChowClass C sX).op (𝟙 X) k 0 _ ≍ α
    rw [TotalChowClass.op_one, gradedCap_one_apply_zero]
    exact (gradedDegreeCast_heq _ _).trans (chowGroupCongr_heq _ _ _ _)

/-- **`ch(𝒪_X) ∩ -` is the identity**: `ch_0(𝒪_X) = 1` and `ch_p(𝒪_X) = 0` for `p > 0`, the
unit of `K_0(Vect(X))` being the class of `𝒪_X`. -/
theorem chernCharacterCap_one : chernCharacterCap C sX 1 = 1 :=
  have := SheafOfModules.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_unit X
  chernCharacterCap_classOf_of_iso_unit C sX _ (Iso.refl _)

end ChernCharacterCap

end Stacks.Chow

